  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-uncertainty question is whether a multimodal fusion of the two strongest encoders (scgpt for RNA, imagenet_vit_l for image) yields a meaningful accuracy gain over unimodal baselines. config_001 tests this in the simplest multimodal setup (singleprofile, concat fusion), establishing a strong reference point. It uses the most capable encoders in the space, so if it performs well, it validates the encoder choices and gives a concrete baseline against which to compare multiprofile aggregation, alternative fusion strategies, and weaker encoders in subsequent experiments. Choosing the simplest multimodal variant first avoids confounding multiple design choices (aggregation + fusion + multiprofile) in a single experiment, maximizing the interpretability of the result for guiding the remaining 9 experiments."
}

